    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFor MLA, the triton backend divides K by `k_scale` before writing the KV cache, because `MLATokenToKVPool` takes no scale: a clone plus a divide on extend and an in-place divide on decode. Quark checkpoints create `k_scale` for every layer and leave it at 1.0 when there is no KV scale, so every layer divides by one.\n\n## Modifications\n\nWhen `k_scale_float == 1.0`, write K directly on both paths. A `None` `k_scale_float` keeps the divide. Non-MLA paths are unchanged.\n\nThis touches the same extend block as #42181 (out-of-place divide) without overlapping it; the two are independent.\n\n## Setup\n\nKimi-K2-Thinking-MXFP4, TP8, MI455X (gfx1250), image `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm10-mi45x-20261011`; aiter is the image's plus ROCm/aiter#5935, #5501, #5043 and #5402 (all in aiter 2bb549102). The Kimi-K2 cookbook targets MI300X; flags used here beyond it: `--attention-backend aiter --prefill-attention-backend aiter --decode-attention-backend triton --page-size 64 --disable-radix-cache --disable-custom-all-reduce --chunked-prefill-size 8192 --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 128`, with `SGLANG_USE_AITER=1`, `SGLANG_ROCM_FUSED_DECODE_MLA=0` and `AITER_FORCE_A8W4=1`. Before and after differ only by this PR.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNumerically identical (division by 1.0). GSM8K with `few_shot_gsm8k` (8-shot, 1319 questions, `max_new_tokens` 512, the settings of sglang's AMD Kimi accuracy tests): before and after to be added.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nDecode at batch 4: the divide was 61 kernels and about 1.2 ms per step; the per-step profile before and after this PR alone is to be added. End to end, TP8 8k/1k concurrency 4: TPOT before and after to be added.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (behaviour unchanged)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (to be added)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38715941475](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38715941475)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38715941366](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38715941366)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38715941426](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38715941426)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
